{
 "rillbook": 1,
 "cells": [
  {
   "name": "about",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "# The idioms book\n\nOne page per ask on the tier-2 simple-things list (`docs/rill-tier2-draft.md`\n\u00a74). Each ask gets a **before** cell \u2014 how it is said with the language as it\nstands \u2014 and, once its operators land, an **after** cell. The pair is the\ncampaign's evidence: the before cell is what the ask cost, the after cell is\nwhat it costs now, and both are parsed by `zig build test` so neither can rot.\n\nRules of the book:\n\n- Every non-markdown cell parses. The gate counts cells both ways, so a cell\n  that stops being collected fails loudly rather than vacuously.\n- An ask that cannot be said at all today has a markdown cell and no before\n  cell. Its beat fills in the after.\n- The mutation for an after cell is deleting the operator it shows off.\n- Paths are the tiltyard's. A cell that reads a path assumes it is seeded\n  before mount \u2014 tick 0 evaluates everything, so a path that does not exist\n  yet is a node that never fires."
  },
  {
   "name": "breathe-ask",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "## Breathe the exposure between 0.5 and 1.5 over four seconds\n\nThe founding example. Scored in \u00a74 as *9 lines, 2 programs, a seed \u2192 1 line*,\nneeding `lfo` and `range`.\n\nTwo programs because \u00a74.4 refuses a program that both writes and subscribes to\none path, and a phase counter is exactly that. A seed because tick 0 evaluates\neverything: `plane.anim.breath.tick` must exist before either program mounts or\nthe reader's nodes never fire.\n\nThe waveform below is a triangle, not a sine \u2014 with no `sin` and no `wave`\nthere is no sine to be had. That is part of what the ask cost."
  },
  {
   "name": "breathe-before-counter",
   "mode": "mounted",
   "markdown": false,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "every 1f | inc plane.anim.breath.tick 1"
  },
  {
   "name": "breathe-before-driver",
   "mode": "mounted",
   "markdown": false,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "plane.anim.breath.tick | div 240 as phase\nphase | floor as whole\nphase | sub whole as frac\nfrac | mul 2 | sub 1 | abs as fold\nfold | mul -1 | add 1 as tri\ntri | lerp 0.5 1.5 | set plane.render.grade.exposure"
  },
  {
   "name": "breathe-after",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "### after \u2014 beat 1a \u2705\n\nOne line. `lfo` is the source, `range` is the exit from the unit interval,\n`set` ends the wave. No counter, no second program, no seed \u2014 and a real\nsine instead of the triangle the arithmetic could reach.\n\nThe mutation that must bite is deleting `lfo`."
  },
  {
   "name": "breathe-after-cell",
   "mode": "mounted",
   "markdown": false,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "lfo sine 4s | range 0.5 1.5 | set plane.render.grade.exposure"
  },
  {
   "name": "elapsed-ask",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "## Show elapsed time on the HUD\n\nThe row `clock` earned for itself. `clock` and `frame` were admitted as\n*substrate* \u2014 they are what `lfo` and the registers are built from \u2014 but\nthe recon noted that admitting them by pin rather than by customer left\nadmission rule 1 with a silent exception. This row closes it honestly."
  },
  {
   "name": "elapsed-after",
   "mode": "mounted",
   "markdown": false,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "clock | set plane.ui.elapsed"
  },
  {
   "name": "flash-ask",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "## Flash a light on an event \u2014 attack and decay, not a rectangle\n\n\u00a74: *~4 lines, and a rectangle \u2192 1*, needing `pulse | ease up down`.\n\nToday the shape is a rectangle because nothing decays: the light goes to full\non the rousing and drops to nothing when the window closes. `delay` moves the\nedge; it does not soften it."
  },
  {
   "name": "flash-before",
   "mode": "mounted",
   "markdown": false,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "plane.signals.horn | set plane.lights.alarm.level 1\nplane.signals.horn | delay 200ms | set plane.lights.alarm.level 0"
  },
  {
   "name": "toggle-ask",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "## Toggle a light on a keypress\n\n\u00a74: *~3 lines \u2192 1*, needing `toggle`.\n\nToday a toggle is a counter through the plane, which costs the second program\nfor the same reason the breathing exposure does \u2014 and the parity test is\narithmetic nobody should have to write."
  },
  {
   "name": "toggle-before-counter",
   "mode": "mounted",
   "markdown": false,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "plane.input.key_l | inc plane.ui.lamp.presses 1"
  },
  {
   "name": "toggle-before-driver",
   "mode": "mounted",
   "markdown": false,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "plane.ui.lamp.presses | div 2 as halved\nhalved | floor | mul 2 as even\nplane.ui.lamp.presses | sub even | = 1 | set plane.lights.lamp.on"
  },
  {
   "name": "count-kills-ask",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "## Count kills\n\n\u00a74: *2 programs (`inc` + reader) \u2192 1*, needing `tally`.\n\n`inc` is the write half and cannot read its own path, so the count is only\nvisible to a second program. `tally` is the same count held inside the\noperator, where the cycle ban does not reach."
  },
  {
   "name": "count-kills-before",
   "mode": "mounted",
   "markdown": false,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "plane.events.kill | inc plane.score.kills 1"
  },
  {
   "name": "night-falls-ask",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "## Night falls, lights on\n\n\u00a74 scores this \u2713 at 1 line today \u2014 and the score is honest about line count\nand wrong about behaviour. `dropped_below` fires on every crossing, so a light\nlevel wobbling either side of the threshold at dusk switches the lights on and\noff repeatedly. This is `above`'s customer (recon \u00a73d), and the row should be\nre-scored *today \u2014 1 line, chatters* when beat 4 lands hysteresis."
  },
  {
   "name": "night-falls-before",
   "mode": "mounted",
   "markdown": false,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "plane.sensors.sky.light | dropped_below 0.3 | set plane.lights.court.on true"
  },
  {
   "name": "fade-in-ask",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "## Fade the exposure in over two seconds on mount\n\n\u00a74: *can't (no register) \u2192 1*, needing `once` and `ramp`.\n\n**Half of it landed in beat 1a.** `ramp` exists, so a fade to a target is\none word; what is still missing is `once` \u2014 a rousing that fires at mount\nand never again. Beat 4. The cell below is the fade with an explicit\ntarget on the plane, which is the honest spelling until `once` lands."
  },
  {
   "name": "fade-in-partial",
   "mode": "mounted",
   "markdown": false,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "plane.render.grade.exposure_target | ramp 2s | set plane.render.grade.exposure"
  },
  {
   "name": "ease-toward-ask",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "## Ease the camera exposure toward a target\n\n\u00a74: *can't \u2192 1*, needing `ease`. No before cell \u2014 same reason."
  },
  {
   "name": "ease-toward-after-note",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "### after \u2014 beat 1a \u2705\n\nThe register chases the target inside the operator, which is legal because\nthe cycle ban is about state through the *plane*. The same idea written\nthrough the plane is still refused at parse."
  },
  {
   "name": "ease-toward-after",
   "mode": "mounted",
   "markdown": false,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "plane.render.grade.exposure_target | ease 400ms | set plane.render.grade.exposure"
  },
  {
   "name": "vu-meter-ask",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "## A VU meter on a field reading\n\n\u00a74: *can't \u2192 1*, needing `abs | ease 20ms down 400ms` \u2014 the envelope\nfollower, which is `ease` with asymmetric time constants. No before cell."
  },
  {
   "name": "vu-meter-after-note",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "### after \u2014 beat 1a \u2705\n\n`ease` with asymmetric constants IS the envelope follower: fast to rise,\nslow to fall. Two keyword ports where the prior art needs three CHOPs."
  },
  {
   "name": "vu-meter-after",
   "mode": "mounted",
   "markdown": false,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "plane.field.rumble | abs | ease 20ms down 400ms | set plane.ui.vu"
  },
  {
   "name": "closing-fast-ask",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "## Alarm when a raider is closing fast, not merely near\n\nProposed \u00a74 row (recon \u00a73e): *invented sensor field \u2192 1*, needing `diff`.\n\nThe probe reviewer invented a `raider_velocity` sensor field because nothing\nin rill derived it. The honest spelling is one word, and it is why `diff`\nearns admission. No before cell: the before was a change to the host."
  },
  {
   "name": "closing-fast-after-note",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "### after \u2014 beat 1a \u2705\n\nOne word where the before was a change to the host. Note the threshold is\nnegative: closing fast is a *falling* distance."
  },
  {
   "name": "closing-fast-after",
   "mode": "mounted",
   "markdown": false,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "plane.sensors.gate.nearest_distance | diff | dropped_below -2 | notify plane.signals.charge"
  },
  {
   "name": "charge-ask",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "## Charge a mechanism while a lever is held, capped\n\nProposed \u00a74 row (recon \u00a73e), landed with the operator. The clamp is\nrequired, not optional: a register's state is saved with the program, so\nan unbounded accumulator is a corpse that gets copied."
  },
  {
   "name": "charge-after",
   "mode": "mounted",
   "markdown": false,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "plane.keep.lever.held | integrate max 100 | set plane.keep.portcullis.charge"
  },
  {
   "name": "swing-ask",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "## Swing a light back and forth\n\n\u00a74: *~8 lines \u2192 1*, needing `lfo tri` and `range`. The before is the breathing\ncounter again with a different output path \u2014 which is the finding: every\nperiodic ask rebuilds the same seven lines."
  },
  {
   "name": "swing-after-note",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "### after \u2014 beat 1a \u2705\n\nThe same three words as the breathing exposure with a different waveform\nand a different sink \u2014 which is the point. Every periodic ask used to\nrebuild the same seven lines of phase arithmetic."
  },
  {
   "name": "swing-after",
   "mode": "mounted",
   "markdown": false,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "lfo tri 8s | shape smooth | range 0 90 | set plane.lights.sweep.angle"
  },
  {
   "name": "cooldown-ask",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "## A cooldown-guarded order\n\n\u00a74 scores this \u2713 at 1 line, and here it is honest \u2014 `cooldown` already holds\nits deadline in op state, which is the mechanism the whole register family\ninherits (recon \u00a70)."
  },
  {
   "name": "cooldown-before",
   "mode": "mounted",
   "markdown": false,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "plane.sensors.gate.enemy_count | rose_above 0 | cooldown 30s | notify plane.orders.muster"
  },
  {
   "name": "rate-limit-ask",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "## Rate-limit a noisy sensor into a knob\n\n\u00a74 scores this \u2713 at 1 line today via `sample`, and names `slew` beside it.\nThe row being already met is why `slew` is *listed, not admitted* (recon \u00a73f)."
  },
  {
   "name": "rate-limit-before",
   "mode": "mounted",
   "markdown": false,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "plane.sensors.hearth.heat | sample 250ms | set plane.render.grade.exposure"
  },
  {
   "name": "dim-lamp-ask",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "## Dim the lamp as the fire dies\n\n\u00a74 scores this \u2713 at 2 lines via fields. Kept in the book as a \u2713 row that the\ncampaign must not regress \u2014 and as one of the two rows flagged in recon \u00a73d as\npossibly \u2713-with-a-wobble against a noisy input."
  },
  {
   "name": "dim-lamp-before",
   "mode": "mounted",
   "markdown": false,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "every 1f { cast $firelight 0.8 radius 6 at plane.sensors.hearth.pos decay 4s }"
  },
  {
   "name": "flicker-ask",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "## Flicker a torch\n\n\u00a74: *can't (no noise) \u2192 1*, needing `noise` and `range`. Beat 4. No before\ncell \u2014 a deterministic flicker cannot be built from the current set at all."
  },
  {
   "name": "drift-ask",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "## Let the grade drift slowly over a minute\n\n\u00a74: *can't \u2192 1*, needing `noise 20s` and `range`. Beat 4."
  },
  {
   "name": "shake-ask",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "## Shake the camera on impact, 300ms\n\n\u00a74: *can't \u2192 2\u20133*, needing `noise` on three seeds, `hold`, and record math.\n`hold` landed in beat 1a; `noise` is beat 4 and record math is beat 1b, so\nthe row does not move yet. Recorded rather than quietly skipped."
  },
  {
   "name": "random-idle-ask",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "## Pick a random idle animation per trigger\n\n\u00a74: *can't \u2192 1*, needing `rand` and `floor`. Beat 4."
  },
  {
   "name": "nearest-hostile-ask",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "## Nearest hostile from the contact list\n\n\u00a74: *invented sensor field \u2192 1*, needing `sort by` and `first`. Beat 3.\nThe contact source publishes an array; today nothing orders one."
  },
  {
   "name": "top-three-ask",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "## Top three threats\n\n\u00a74: *can't \u2192 1*, needing `sort by` and `take`. Beat 3."
  },
  {
   "name": "three-points-ask",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "## Move a light through three points typed into a cell\n\n\u00a74: *host verb only \u2192 1*, needing the array literal and `along`. Beats 2 and 3.\nThis is the ask the rillbook exists for: three points typed into a cell, no\nhost verb in the way."
  },
  {
   "name": "time-of-day-ask",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "## Pick an exposure by time-of-day band\n\n\u00a74: *`select` chain \u2192 1*, needing the array literal and `choose`. Beat 2."
  },
  {
   "name": "time-of-day-before",
   "mode": "mounted",
   "markdown": false,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "plane.world.hour | < 6 as night\nplane.world.hour | < 18 as day\nnight | select 0.2 1.0 as lit\nday | select lit 0.4 | set plane.render.grade.exposure"
  },
  {
   "name": "follow-ask",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "## Keep a light two metres above the player\n\n\u00a74: *~3 lines \u2192 1\u20132*, needing record math (the broadcast pin). Recon \u00a76 argues\nthis lands in beat 1b rather than beat 2, because broadcast is one change to\none comptime helper and every math word should be born with it."
  },
  {
   "name": "follow-before",
   "mode": "mounted",
   "markdown": false,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "plane.entities.player.pos.y | add 2 as lifted\n{x: plane.entities.player.pos.x, y: lifted, z: plane.entities.player.pos.z}\n  | set plane.lights.follow.pos"
  },
  {
   "name": "follow-after-note",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "### after \u2014 beat 1b \u2705\n\nMath is elementwise over records, so a position plus an offset is the\nsentence. No vector family, no rebuilt record, no separate `map`.\n\nThe mutation that must bite is making `add` scalar again."
  },
  {
   "name": "follow-after",
   "mode": "mounted",
   "markdown": false,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "plane.entities.player.pos | add {x: 0, y: 2, z: 0} | set plane.lights.follow.pos"
  },
  {
   "name": "contracts-ask",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "## Refuse a malformed contact list, and pin what a program reads\n\n\u00a74's last two rows: both *silent \u2192 1*, needing `match` (runtime) and `expect`\n(mount). Beat 2. There is no before cell because \"silent\" is the before: a\nshape mismatch today is discovered downstream, or not at all."
  },
  {
   "name": "ticking-ask",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "## What movement costs, and how to see it\n\nEverything downstream of `clock`, `frame` or `lfo` re-evaluates every\ntick \u2014 that is the cost of animation, and it is meant to be visible\nrather than discovered. `OpDef.ticks` declares which operators may\nre-arm themselves; the console lights a badge from it and shows the\nnode's **live evaluation count** beside it. The badge says what could\ncost; the counter says what did.\n\nA register is the interesting case: it ticks *while converging* and then\nstops, so its badge is lit and its counter goes flat. The cell below\nconverges and then costs nothing, which is the property the whole family\nrests on \u2014 and there is a gate that watches the counter stop."
  },
  {
   "name": "ticking-demo",
   "mode": "mounted",
   "markdown": false,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "plane.target | ease 100ms | set plane.smoothed"
  },
  {
   "name": "broadcast-refusals",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "## What broadcast refuses, and how it says so\n\nBroadcast and its mismatch check landed together \u2014 ratified up front,\nbecause ICE shipped broadcast without one and that error was the thing\nevery ICE user learned to dread.\n\nEvery refusal names the operator, **both sides**, and where, in a\ntype-word vocabulary defined once (`number`, `record{x, y}`, `[number]`)\nand reused by beat 2's shape literal:\n\n```\nadd: record{x, y, z} and record{x, y} \u2014 field 'z' is missing on the right\nadd: [number] of 3 and [number] of 2 \u2014 arrays must be the same length\nadd: record{x, y} and [number] \u2014 a record and an array have no elementwise meaning\nmul: the left side is string, not a number at .inner.name \u2014 record{inner} and number\n```\n\nThere is no implicit intersection and no zip-to-the-shorter. Picking a\nrule quietly is how a wrong answer learns to look like a right one.\n\nThe cells below are the two that broadcast *replaced*: `window | mul`\nIS map, and a comparator over an array is the predicate beat 3's `keep`\nwill filter on."
  },
  {
   "name": "broadcast-map",
   "mode": "mounted",
   "markdown": false,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "plane.gpu.traversal_ms | window 10s | mul 2 | stats | set plane.ui.load"
  },
  {
   "name": "broadcast-predicate",
   "mode": "mounted",
   "markdown": false,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "plane.sensors.gate.contacts | > 0 | set plane.ui.any_contact"
  },
  {
   "name": "range-not-lerp",
   "mode": "query",
   "markdown": true,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "## `range` or `lerp`?\n\nThe same arithmetic \u2014 `lo + (hi \u2212 lo) \u00b7 t` \u2014 and one difference that\nearns the second word: **`range` clamps, `lerp` extrapolates.**\n\nEverything upstream of a modulation chain (`lfo`, `wave`, `shape`)\nleaves 0..1 by construction, and `range` is the **exit** from that\ninterval: if a source ever strays, the exposure stays inside the range\nyou named instead of going dark or blowing out. Reach for `lerp` when\nyou are genuinely blending two things and want to be able to overshoot.\n\nRatified as built, 2026-08-25."
  },
  {
   "name": "range-exit",
   "mode": "mounted",
   "markdown": false,
   "collapsed": false,
   "source": "lfo sine 4s | shape smooth | range 0.5 1.5 | set plane.render.grade.exposure"
  }
 ]
}